  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resistance of heating element after temperature increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>220</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>110</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;(from Ohm&#39;s law). The new resistance is related to the temperature coefficient of the heating element as&nbsp;<math><mn>110</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>500</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
